  "limitations": [
    "A classifier estimates a probability; it does not guarantee detection. Expect false positives and false negatives on real traffic.",
    "Metrics reflect the training distribution. A lab dataset is not a production network: expect degradation under concept drift.",
    "Verify every alert against the underlying evidence before acting.",
    "Classifiers trained on encrypted or anonymised flows (e.g. some published CSV releases) see less signal than production captures.",
    "UNSW-NB15 is a hybrid corpus: the authors combined real modern normal traffic with synthetic contemporary attack behaviours generated by the IXIA PerfectStorm tool in a cyber range. It is real published research data, not production captures, so accuracy here is an upper bound rather than a field estimate.",
    "UNSW-NB15 releases flow *statistics*, not payloads and not IP addresses or ports, so the model cannot see the indicators an analyst would actually use.",
